  "content_json": {
    "id": "tr-a1-future",
    "cefr": "A1",
    "title": "Future tense: -(y)AcAk",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "what-is-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The suffix "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-(y)AcAk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " is Turkish's dedicated future-tense marker. It attaches to a verb stem and, together with a personal ending, states that an action will happen. The capital letters signal vowel harmony: the suffix surfaces as "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-acak"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " after back vowels (a, ı, o, u) and as "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-ecek"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " after front vowels (e, i, ö, ü). The parenthesised "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-y-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " is a buffer consonant inserted only when the stem ends in a vowel."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "what is it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "when-to-use-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Planned future actions."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Use -(y)AcAk for anything you intend or expect to happen: appointments, schedules, decisions already made."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Predictions."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " When you predict an outcome — based on evidence or general expectation — -(y)AcAk is the natural choice."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Not a substitute for present continuous."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Turkish speakers do not routinely use the present-continuous -(I)yor to express future plans the way English does. When the event is clearly future, -(y)AcAk is more idiomatic."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "when to use it"
      },
      {
        "id": "formation",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The structure is: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "verb stem + (y) + acak/ecek + personal ending"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". Two phonological rules apply before you add the personal ending."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Buffer -y-."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " If the stem ends in a vowel, insert "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-y-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " between the stem and the suffix: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "bekle-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "bekleyecek"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "; "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "oku-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "okuyacak"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "k → ğ softening."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " The suffix ends in "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-k"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". When a vowel-initial personal ending follows (1sg "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-im"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ", 1pl "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-iz"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "), that "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-k"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " softens to "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-ğ"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ": "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "gelecek + im"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "geleceğim"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Negative."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Insert the negative morpheme "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-mA-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " between the stem and the future suffix. Vowel harmony applies: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "gel-me-yecek"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "gelmeyecek"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "; "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "yap-ma-yacak"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "yapmayacak"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". The "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-A-"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " of -mA harmonises with the front/back quality of the stem's last vowel, not the suffix."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
